Earpiece F-008/F-010: frame log and headless replay mode for the Police-911 PCSX2 fork.
Applies on top of pcsx2-vr.patch (the pcsx2-vr tree: stock v2.6.3 + pcsx2-vr.patch), with or
without F-009's pcsx2-knobs.patch, in either order. Byte for byte (PINE.cpp, QtHost.cpp,
Counters.cpp and the vcxproj are CRLF, the VR files LF): see .gitattributes.
F-010 (2026-11-03): finished against the real tree; `git apply --check` passes there, and
Replay.cpp, PINE.cpp, VRSession.cpp, Counters.cpp and QtHost.cpp compile with MSVC (Release
AVX2). Build and run per earpiece RIG_CHECKLIST "F-010".

  cd pcsx2-vr; git apply ../vr/pcsx2-replay.patch     then build Release AVX2 as usual

What it adds (opcodes match earpiece-rig/src/earpiece_rig/pine.py):
- 0x40 MsgFrameLog, every fork build: reply u32 n, then n x (u32 g_FrameCount, u64
  QueryPerformanceCounter in ns, the clock Python's perf_counter_ns reads), the vsyncs since
  the last ask (ring of 1024). No VM needed.
- 0x42 MsgFrameCount: u32 g_FrameCount now.
- 0x41 MsgReplayStep: only in a -earpiece-replay instance, and only while paused; FAIL
  otherwise, so Todd's game can never be driven by it. Payload 132 bytes: head, left hand,
  right hand, each u32 buttons, f32 trigger, thumb x, thumb y, f32 pos[3], f32 quat[4] (x y z w).
  Holds the head pose as the VR camera input, runs exactly one frame with PCSX2's frame
  advance, waits until the CPU thread has stopped again, replies u32 g_FrameCount.
- -earpiece-replay <port> -earpiece-data <absolute dir>: refuses to start (stderr, exit 1) if
  the port is 28011/28012 or the folder is missing, relative or overlaps PCSX2's own folder.
  Copies Todd's PCSX2.ini (read only) to <dir>/inis and from then on uses only <dir> for
  everything it writes (ini, sstates, memcards, cache, logs, per-game settings); BIOS,
  patches, cheats and textures are read from Todd's folders by absolute path. Overrides:
  memory cards off, Null renderer, Null audio, no window (surfaceless), VR Mode dryrun (never
  loads openvr_api.dll), all input sources off, MTVU off (determinism), PINE on <port>,
  achievements off, starts paused.

